course: dictionary
lesson: 360
title: Anthem: a special song
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An anthem is a song that is special to a country or a group, and people often sing it together at big events. Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «When the national anthem is played, you stand still and quiet.» The sentence tells you that an anthem is played at important moments, and people stand still and quiet while it plays.
explain: The word national in «national anthem» is a clue too: a national anthem belongs to a whole country. Sports matches and ceremonies are other clues, because those are the places where anthems are played.
explain: Anthem can have other meanings. It can be a religious song sung in church by a choir, or a popular song that many people love to sing together. The context tells you which meaning fits. Check your choice by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: An anthem is a song that is special to a country or group.
fact: «National anthem» means the song of a whole country.
fact: «Stand for the anthem» means to stand up while it is sung or played, to show respect.
fact: Examples of national anthems include «God Save the King» (UK), «The Star-Spangled Banner» (USA), «O Canada» and «Advance Australia Fair» (Australia).
fact: An anthem can also mean a religious song sung in church, often by a choir.
exercise: «When the national anthem is played, you stand still and quiet.» What is an anthem? | *A song that is special to a country, sung at big events | A type of school lunch | Something you wear on your head | A kind of flag
exercise: «At solemn moments, like a funeral or the national anthem, you stand still and quiet to show respect.» What do people usually do when the national anthem is played? | Run to the front of the room | Leave the room straight away | Dance in the aisles | *Stand still and quiet
exercise: The word national in «national anthem» tells you the song belongs to what? | *A whole country | A single family | A sports team only | A shop
test: «The choir sang an anthem in the church on Sunday.» What kind of anthem is this most likely? | *A religious song | A national flag | A popular pop song | A map of the town
test: «The crowd sang the anthem together as the flag went up.» Which thing is the anthem most like? | A recipe for cake | A type of bird | *A song for a whole country | A map of the sea
exam: Which sentence about anthems is true? | An anthem is always a dance | Anthems are only spoken, never sung | An anthem is a kind of building | *An anthem is a song that is special to a country or group
